# Input transport and recorded candidate workflow

This held Source preparation performs no command, project import, input
conversion, Cargo build, observer call, comparison, publication or gate update.
Only Root may invoke these scripts after actual Native05 custody release and
independent formatter/quality08 review. Future output identities are operands.

`write_request.py` requires these options:

```
--approved-source-sha256 WRITER_SHA --source-manifest PREP#SHA
--native-freeze FREEZE#SHA --formatted-inventory INVENTORY#SHA
--quality QUALITY08#SHA --conversion-ledger LEDGER#SHA
--conversion-execution RECORDER_RECEIPT#SHA --output-dir FRESH_DIRECTORY
```

It validates the exact twelve applied bodies from b089/f4d6/beef, their held
literal archives and current formatted archives, both ordered runtime bindings,
and all four actual successful quality commands with the same full raw Source
snapshot. Recorder snapshot references may omit size; supplied sizes remain
mandatory exact checks. Current source membership, every archive and every
current Rust/Cargo byte are checked independently of narrow API bindings.

The Native05 freeze supplies exact direct6, admission12 and literal input refs.
The one genuine SCH input conversion must join the frozen IDF, unchanged staged
IDF, available epJSON, converter Source archives, ledger and recorded stdout.
Its declared input-only/non-scientifically-frozen scope is retained. No manual
ReportInputs, geometry, timestep, Native answer or result is accepted. The writer
emits the observer's exact twelve-key request and separate input custody record.

`run_candidates.py` takes all the same options, plus:

```
--production-request REQUEST15#SHA
--production-projection-execution PROJECTOR_RECEIPT#SHA
```

It authenticates the existing reviewed projector03 invocation and request, then
records the direct writer in a fresh child directory. One Cargo build with both
`--example` arguments captures the actual emitted production and direct binaries.
Both source closures must match the full quality snapshot. Each binary is called
once with its separate request path and SHA (argc3), under distinct receipts.
Actual exit 0 or 2 is retained; the workflow returns 2 if either observer returns
2. A compile/launch/custody failure stops without rerun or correction. No observer
stdout numerical values are parsed, compared or supplied to the other lane.

All outputs are fresh children of `.runtime/porting/CTF-10`. The workflow stores
actual writer/build/candidate identities and rechecks full sources, inputs and
executables. Success here means recorded execution custody only. Numerical,
whole-Init and integration parity require their separate reviewed comparison;
this preparation claims none. Native historical source documents are validated
through sealed refs; old live plan/card paths are not recursively rebound.
